rum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1122743-haberdasher-s-requiem-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\">Haberdasher's Requiem Conversions and Homebrew</span></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6498-haberdasher","name":"Haberdasher","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6498_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"818"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T20:38:22-07:00","id":1148978,"title":"","content":"Or Inguma taking on Lovecraftian-horrors in general.<br /> <br /> Either way, hype is real for Beast PG.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T20:50:27-07:00","id":1148981,"title":"","content":"Talassii sounds very neat and possibly more fitting than an npc I have classified as a Namtaru that chases people around in an enclosed space.<br /> <br /> Not quite sure what Inguma means for &quot;fear of The Other&quot;. Is it a more of a straight forward Freddy Krueger-esque family that represents the fear of going to sleep?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5557-runcible","name":"Runcible","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5557_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"164"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T20:52:09-07:00","id":1148982,"title":"","content":"Fear of the Other could go some really uncomfortable places. Hoping for a delicate touch with that one.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T20:56:53-07:00","id":1148984,"title":"","content":"A Hunger that revolves around societal taboos?<br /> <br /> Yes, please!<br /> <br /> <br /> I can totally see this as the Beast providing others with the means to break away from tradition and expectations, before sending anonymous tips to those in charge of investigating such activities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>blackhatmatt</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1148961#post1148961\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The new Families are the Inguma (Nightmares of the Other) and the Talassii (Nightmares of Confinement).<br /> <br /> Thanks, and good night! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, I've got a general idea of what form an Inguma might take (somebody from another world / culture?)<br /> <br /> But how does one play as an avatar of confinement? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1148971#post1148971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know a lot of people have been using Makara to represent dangerous, inescapable places... looks like the Talassii could be butting in on that.<br /> <br /> Inguma whose Horror takes the form of a Xenomorph, anyone?</div> </div> </div> </div>I saw the Makara as being the fear of getting dropped into an environment you aren't suited to. Like somebody from a wealthy gated community waking up to find themselves dumped in the back alley streets of the downtown ghetto.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-12-2017, 12:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T21:37:54-07:00","id":1148991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1148984#post1148984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I've got a general idea of what form an Inguma might take (somebody from another world / culture?)</div> </div> </div> </div>'The monster races.' I'd imagine it can be people from other cultures or areas just like it could be something from outside a person's general understanding, like greys or Slenderman. One of the benefits of the open nature of the fears, I think.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But how does one play as an avatar of confinement? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> </div> </div> </div>Aside from the obvious being imprisoned physically, things like 'You signed a contract and I have a law firm at my disposal,&quot; or &quot;You work for me, and with one phone call I can make sure no one else will ever hire you.&quot; I remember an X-files episode where an AI made agent Mulder think he had his legs amputated, potentially keeping him from going anywhere. Or a simple, '<a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B01B084B50/\" target=\"_blank\">I love you and there's nothing you can do about it</a>' type of stalker who just won't give up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T22:04:09-07:00","id":1148997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1148991#post1148991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Aside from the obvious being imprisoned physically, things like 'You signed a contract and I have a law firm at my disposal,&quot; or &quot;You work for me, and with one phone call I can make sure no one else will ever hire you.&quot; I remember an X-files episode where an AI made agent Mulder think he had his legs amputated, potentially keeping him from going anywhere. Or a simple, '<a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B01B084B50/\" target=\"_blank\">I love you and there's nothing you can do about it</a>' type of stalker who just won't give up.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I also vaguely recall that episode. And I am reminded of that movie where a writer is held captive by his 'biggest fan' while she forces him to rewrite his latest book, because she doesn't like the way it ended.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T22:44:34-07:00","id":1149001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1148984#post1148984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But how does one play as an avatar of confinement? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/eek.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"EEK!\" smilieid=\"9\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Gerald\u2019s Game. Misery. The Mist. Cabin in the Woods. Cloverfield Lane. Evil Dead. Saw. The Shining. The Haunting of Hill House. House of Leaves. Arabian Nights. <br /> <br /> Just a few points of inspiration off the top of my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-11T22:45:56-07:00","id":1149003,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1148982#post1148982\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fear of the Other could go some really uncomfortable places. Hoping for a delicate touch with that one.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, Beast has kinda already gone there.<br /> <br /> We do already have a Dark Era for Beast set in Reconstruction South, which fully admits that &quot;Yeah, there were Beasts on both sides and who are REALLY passionate about defending their sides&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T00:44:22-07:00","id":1149021,"title":"","content":"The Hype is real. Both new families are nice, though I have to admit that the Hunger for Transgression is more than epic: It is necessary. That it PERFECTLY fits my Therapist-Makara who is somewhere between Hannibal and Will Graham has nothing to do with this assessment, why do you ask? =P<br /> <br /> No seriously. Beast in general is a very neat exploration of Monster Theory, and one thing that has been a bit missing so far was the instigator role, the tempter-monster that causes monstrousness in others. Well, no more. Kudos!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T00:59:00-07:00","id":1149024,"title":"","content":"Thanks Matt for the news! At the risk of sounding mechanics obsessed, I'm really eager to see what Atavisms those guys come in with - if only because this will open nice new combinations with the other existing Families.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10272-daigotsu-max","name":"Daigotsu Max","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10272_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"322"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T01:01:28-07:00","id":1149025,"title":"","content":"Here here, <br /> <br /> Couldn't agree more with the sentiments being presented here. Plus this upcoming weekend is my tabletop gaming group's two year anniversary for our own Beast: the Primordial Chronicle, so the reveal of the two new Families and new Hunger will generate much hype at our get together. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3436-dusksage","name":"Dusksage","avatar":"