xual, just the ones who try to throw off suspicion by ripping on others.<br /> <br /> In other words, they'd feed on hypocrites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, you said precisely none of that, you just said they feed off closeted homosexuals. Feel free to act defensive, but you could also just apologize and say the base concept was in poor taste.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T21:06:41-07:00","id":1149304,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149302#post1149302\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Okay, you said precisely none of that, you just said they feed off closeted homosexuals. Feel free to act defensive, but you could also just apologize and say the base concept was in poor taste.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>I strongly advise you</b> to read my post before throwing accusations my way. I specifically said closet homosexuals who go out of their way to chastise and humiliate those who are openly gay. You can even check my post up there to see that I haven't recently edited it.<br /> <br /> You must have misinterpreted my meaning.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T21:18:07-07:00","id":1149305,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149304#post1149304\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I specifically said closet homosexuals who go out of their way to chastise and humiliate those who are openly gay.[\u2026]<br /> <br /> You must have misinterpreted my meaning.</div> </div> </div> </div>You also specifically said that they'd be subjected to the same behavior that they engaged in. Quit while you're behind, Nyr.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T21:38:09-07:00","id":1149308,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149305#post1149305\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You also specifically said that they'd be subjected to the same behavior that they engaged in. Quit while you're behind, Nyr.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> No, I specifically said they'd be subjected to the same mistreatment they gave others. Meaning that if somebody is gay, but refuses to admit they're gay, while at the same time going around and making fun of people for being gay, then the Enabler tricks them into a scenario where they reveal their secret gayness, then displays it for everybody to find out.<br /> <br /> And that's a bad thing, how?<br /> <br /> They go around tearing other people down for something they themselves are guilty of, and then when they're on the receiving end of it, that's somehow bad?<br /> <br /> That sounds exactly like what a good Nemesis should be trying to achieve. Exposing their victims to the same abuse they've inflicted upon others for so long.<br /> <br /> Sorry, but if I'm falling behind in this discussion (I wouldn't call it a debate), I seriously need somebody to clarify why.<br /> <br /> <br /> Also, like I said, I specifically said the phrase <i>&quot;such as&quot; </i>- meaning that closet homosexuals aren't even the primary focus of their targets. <b>They go after hypocrites.</b> Meaning, anybody who tells you not to do something, but then goes and does it themselves when they think nobody's watching.<br /> <br /> That's what they'd be trying to expose to the public. Not what kind of gender you prefer to involve yourself with.<br /> <br /> <br /> To be honest, I actually expected a reaction kind of like this, when I proposed the character idea. Which is why I tried to clarify my meaning as much as possible. Atamajakki simply misread my post and picked up on something that wasn't there. They even said that my (and I quote) <i>&quot;entire character concept is stigmatizing homosexuality.&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Which could not be any further from the truth; that is a colossal leap from anything I actually wrote. I'm looking right at my original post, I've read through it more than 6 times. I do not see any connotations that might be considered offensive to people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-13-2017, 02:48 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T22:17:36-07:00","id":1149315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149308#post1149308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They go around tearing other people down for something they themselves are guilty of, and then when they're on the receiving end of it, that's somehow bad?</div> </div> </div> </div>It is, in fact, generally considered extremely poor form to out someone with the specific goal of seeing them ridiculed and ostracized, Nyr.<br /> <br /> Applying &quot;exposing hypocrites&quot; to the specific example of internalized homophobia \u2014 the example of what this character preys upon that you specifically chose to present \u2014 cannot be done without perpetrating the risk of violence predicated upon the knowledge of a person's sexual preference.<br /> <br /> This isn't &quot;Boss Richman keeps telling his employees to be frugal, but his employees have just learned he spends thirty-thousand dollars a week on decadent secret society bacchanalia,&quot; this is &quot;Ted the Homophobe Who Hangs Out With Other Homophobes keeps saying gay people are going to hell and deserve to have the shit beat out of them, but his homophobe buddies have just learned he slept with a dude on his own initiative while completely sober and in control of his own faculties.&quot; &quot;The public&quot; is not confined to big-hearted people who will limit themselves to scathing remarks \u2014 this is stuff that gets used to fuel mob violence.<br /> <br /> This isn't a matter of offense, this is a matter of using <b>&quot;exploit and expose the phenomenon of closeted homophobes&quot;</b> as part of the elevator pitch for what is otherwise a fairly standard narrative leveraged by a Beast who feeds from getting people to break their own rules. It's careless and tone-deaf and &quot;I didn't mean it like that&quot; doesn't change the outcome here any more than it does accidentally running over the neighbor kid's pet dog. You lose nothing by apologizing for the mistake.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T22:25:30-07:00","id":1149316,"title":"","content":"Presumably along with the Nightmares of Confinement will be some abilities revolving around exerting social pressure, too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T22:35:30-07:00","id":1149321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149315#post1149315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It is, in fact, generally considered extremely poor form to out someone with the specific goal of seeing them ridiculed and ostracized, Nyr.<br /> <br /> Applying &quot;exposing hypocrites&quot; to the specific example of internalized homophobia \u2014 the example of what this character preys upon that you specifically chose to present \u2014 cannot be done without perpetrating the risk of violence predicated upon the knowledge of a person's sexual preference.<br /> <br /> This isn't &quot;Boss Richman keeps telling his employees to be frugal, but his employees have just learned he spends thirty-thousand dollars a week on decadent secret society bacchanalia,&quot; this is &quot;Ted the Homophobe Who Hangs Out With Other Homophobes keeps saying gay people are going to hell and deserve to have the shit beat out of them, but his homophobe buddies have just learned he slept with a dude on his own initiative while completely sober and in control of his own faculties.&quot; &quot;The public&quot; is not confined to big-hearted people who will limit themselves to scathing remarks \u2014 this is stuff that gets used to fuel mob violence.<br /> <br /> This isn't a matter of offense, this is a matter of using <b>&quot;exploit and expose the phenomenon of closeted homophobes&quot;</b> as part of the elevator pitch for what is otherwise a fairly standard narrative leveraged by a Beast who feeds from getting people to break their own rules. It's careless and tone-deaf and &quot;I didn't mean it like that&quot; doesn't change the outcome here any more than it does accidentally running over the neighbor kid's pet dog. You lose nothing by apologizing for the mistake.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Even if I did apologize, it wouldn't be sincere. Basically, this is the same scenario as somebody who apologizes once they've been found guilty of a crime. They're not sorry they did something wrong, they're sorry they got caught.<br /> <br /> But I want to clarify that I don't see my post as being wrong, which is why the apology would be insincere. In my eyes, if you're the kind of person who goes around abusing other people just so that a bunch of a-holes won't turn their attentions on you, then you get no sympathy from me. I have known these kinds of people personally. I have even been the subject of their mistreatments through the entirety of my youth. <i>My own brother was among them!</i><br /> <br /> So no, I will not apologize for a character concept that revolves around dishing out a little payback to these kinds of people.<br /> <br /> <br /> What I will do, however, is admit that I could have chosen a better example than closest homosexuals. I just couldn't think of one at the time, so I wrote the first one that came to my head. Thinking about it now, my original post could have made its point just as clearly as if I simply used the term 'hypocrites', instead of giving a specific example. If you'd like me to edit my post to something like that, I'd be happy to do so, before this explodes into something entirely unnecessary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-13-2017, 01:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T23:07:47-07:00","id":1149325,"title":"","content":"Regardless of intent or motivation, a character who exists to ruin people by outing them - even if those people are monstrous! - is awful and offfensive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T23:24:33-07:00","id":1149326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149321#post1149321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I could have chosen a better example than closest homosexuals. I just couldn't think of one at the time, so I wrote the first one that came to my head. Thinking about it now, my original post could have made its point just as clearly as if I simply used the term 'hypocrites', instead of giving a specific example. If you'd like me to edit my post to something like that, I'd be happy to do so, before this explodes into something entirely unnecessary.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:Red\">No. The fact that you said,</span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149308#post1149308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I actually expected a reaction kind of like this, when I proposed the character idea.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">Clearly indicates that you were fully aware this example would likely result in empassioned responses, but chose to use that example anyway, which makes the example a violation of rule 2.</span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149321#post1149321\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if I did apologize, it wouldn't be sincere. Basically, this is the same scenario as somebody who apologizes once they've been found guilty of a crime. They're not sorry they did something wrong, they're sorry they got caught.<br /> <br /> But I want to clarify that I don't see my post as being wrong, which is why the apology would be insincere.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">Not that an apology would have made this any less of a rules violation, but this clearly indicates that you are not going to learn anything from an infraction. Usually, when the mods suspect disciplinary action won't lead to a change in behavior, we issue a permanent ban. I'm going to give you this chance, however, to drop this subject now. I don't care if you think you did anything wrong in bringing up the concept or not, but bring it up again and you're done.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T23:39:59-07:00","id":1149331,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149326#post1149326\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:red\">Not that an apology would have made this any less of a rules violation, but this clearly indicates that you are not going to learn anything from an infraction. Usually, when the mods suspect disciplinary action won't lead to a change in behavior, we issue a permanent ban. I'm going to give you this chance, however, to drop this subject now. I don't care if you think you did anything wrong in bringing up the concept or not, but bring it up again and you're done.</span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Fine, subject dropped. Didn't mean for it to get this out of hand, anyways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-12T23:53:21-07:00","id":1149333,"title":"","content":"To change the subject somewhat, what kinds of Horrors would people expect from the new Hungers? Transgression lends itself well to tempters (succubi, sirens and so on), of course, but what shapes would a fear of the Other take? Would there be lots of 'uncanny valley' situations, with beings that are almost human but not quite? Like, for example, the AI from <i>Ex Machina</i> and such?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T00:28:27-07:00","id":1149336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149333#post1149333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Transgression lends itself well to tempters (succubi, sirens and so on), of course, but what shapes would a fear of the Other take? Would there be lots of 'uncanny valley' situations, with beings that are almost human but not quite? Like, for example, the AI from <i>Ex Machina</i> and such?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Other nicely can come up with Lovecraftian 'Innsmouth look', etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T00:48:08-07:00","id":1149338,"title":"","content":"Dopplegangers seem like a good fear of others. Really peeve off the Unchained too if they had a power that let them appear to be others.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T00:55:50-07:00","id":1149339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149333#post1149333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To change the subject somewhat, what kinds of Horrors would people expect from the new Hungers? Transgression lends itself well to tempters (succubi, sirens and so on), of course, but what shapes would a fear of the Other take? Would there be lots of 'uncanny valley' situations, with beings that are almost human but not quite? Like, for example, the AI from <i>Ex Machina</i> and such?</div> </div> </div> </div>I should point out that Fear of the Other is one of the new <i>Families</i>, the other of which is Fear of Confinement. The second new Hunger is the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1012827-family-and-hunger-that-fit-perfectly?p=1014710#post1014710\">Hunger for Secrets</a>.<br /> <br /> Both axes have their influence on the Horror's form, of course, but the particulars are different for &quot;what it eats&quot; versus &quot;what it is.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T01:01:15-07:00","id":1149340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149339#post1149339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I should point out that Fear of the Other is one of the new <i>Families</i>, the other of which is Fear of Confinement. The second new Hunger is the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1012827-family-and-hunger-that-fit-perfectly?p=1014710#post1014710\">Hunger for Secrets</a>.<br /> <br /> Both axes have their influence on the Horror's form, of course, but the particulars are different for &quot;what it eats&quot; versus &quot;what it is.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh. Whoops. I think I got confused there. Apologies. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T01:43:19-07:00","id":1149345,"title":"","content":"How about Body Snatchers, almost-humanlike animals, slenderman and other similar uncanny valley people? Basically most of what Horror movies developed during the Red Scare is probably a valid inspiration, as a lot of it was coloured by that Fear of the Other.<br /> <br /> While you could probably tackle tons of racism or ideology stuff with the Inguma, and I can see them take any side of that particular 'debate', I think the Other doesn't even have to be an outright monster (Deep One Hybrids for example) or somehow different, but rather be 'off' in a significant way. Like Hannibal and similar criminals are to us. But also any situation where sharing space with a stranger is uncomfortable, but dialed up to eleven, basically.<br /> <br /> Lessons aplenty, from forcing people to broaden their horizon (not a nice thing to do at all) to making people question their own customs, all through to reinforcing existing customs and narrowing their horizon (&quot;Don't talk to strangers&quot; is a valid lesson. An Inguma Collector could easily come to the conclusion that teaching this is important, and that kidnapping people is a valid way of teaching it).<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T02:51:52-07:00","id":1149353,"title":"","content":"Inguma will be great for all the Islamo- and Homophobic tension in Center and Western Europe - just saying as man living in Poland...<br /> <br /> I will also use Inguma extensively in <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1125616-fan-dark-era-conquest-of-paradise-age-of-exploration\">Conquest of Paradise</a></b> fan Dark Era - as people of future Spain and Portugal were <i>very terrified </i>of Muslims and Jews in their ranks. Original Spanish Inquisition was looking for Jews in first place, general heretics as second.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 10-13-2017, 07:53 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T04:40:55-07:00","id":1149360,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149300#post1149300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, not sure how much I love the idea of a Beast whose <i>entire character concept</i> is stigmatizing homosexuality.</div> </div> </div> </div> It sounds like an ideal antagonist to me. I wouldn't want to play him, but I if he showed up as an antagonist I think it could easily be an enemy I'd love to hate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T05:25:54-07:00","id":1149367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ajf115</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149333#post1149333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To change the subject somewhat, what kinds of Horrors would people expect from the new Hungers? ... what shapes would a fear of the Other take? Would there be lots of 'uncanny valley' situations, with beings that are almost human but not quite? Like, for example, the AI from <i>Ex Machina</i> and such?</div> </div> </div> </div>The earlier idea of appearing as multiple copies of yourself might work for a Horror form rather than an Atavism or Nightmare - manage to manifest your Lair and you surround everyone.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me, is the Player's Guide coming with new Lair Traits as well?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T05:31:43-07:00","id":1149370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149367#post1149367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The earlier idea of appearing as multiple copies of yourself might work for a Horror form rather than an Atavism or Nightmare - manage to manifest your Lair and you surround everyone.<br /> <br /> Which reminds me, is the Player's Guide coming with new Lair Traits as well?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think I proposed a Beast in the Concept thread whose body is made up of tiny, compacted mirrors that reflects the image of whoever is looking at them. They pretended to be the victim's guilty conscience by tormenting people in their dreams with memories of their misdeeds. I don't remember what family they were (Namtaru, or Eshmaki, probably), but now it sounds like there's one just perfect for them!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T05:56:51-07:00","id":1149375,"title":"","content":"Hmm... thinking more. Is there going to be a Fear of Infection Family? Because there's some nasty things you could do with that, like Nazism themed antagonists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T06:06:59-07:00","id":1149379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149375#post1149375\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm... thinking more. Is there going to be a Fear of Infection Family? Because there's some nasty things you could do with that, like Nazism themed antagonists.</div> </div> </div> </div>Don\u2019t existing Atavisms already pretty strongly tie that as an aspect of the Gorgons?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T06:22:46-07:00","id":1149383,"title":"","content":"I'd say it's a modest connection not a strong one, and the actual splat write up doesn't cover the idea.<br /> <br /> To give a concrete example. Count Dracula. Specifically the way he ties into Victorian sexual norms and the fear of becoming a &quot;fallen woman&quot;. He's handsome, he's charming, and once he seduces you then you're infected and turn into a vampire.<br /> <br /> I'm not sure you could really do handsome and charming for a Gorgon. Count Orlok on the other hand...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":134,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","user":"The Kings Raven","date":". 10-13-2017, 09:27 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T07:22:29-07:00","id":1149402,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149383#post1149383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm not sure you could really do handsome and charming for a Gorgon.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You absolutely could. The concept of being a Gorgon is that they make people feel uncomfortable. While the obvious stereotype is that the Gorgon themselves are the ones who are repulsive, you could also invert the trope by making the Gorgon so alluring, that their victims become disgusted at themselves for not being as popular as they are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T07:35:28-07:00","id":1149403,"title":"","content":"I have always found that to be a weird interpretation of the Gorgons. I feel like Alluring is more Makara. Gorgons should not be pretty, or popular, imo. Famous, sure, succesful and envied, no problem. But not 'popular' as in 'adored, has fans, is admired as a person', But then, that's just me, I guess.<br /> <br /> The fear of becoming 'infected' (e.g. the aforementioned 'fallen woman') is different from disgust. So I can definitly see potential there.<br /> For now, I am more curious about that Hunger for Secrets, which sounds like THE go-to Hunger for the stereotypical Ugallu for me so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T08:12:16-07:00","id":1149417,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149383#post1149383\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To give a concrete example. Count Dracula. Specifically the way he ties into Victorian sexual norms and the fear of becoming a &quot;fallen woman&quot;. He's handsome, he's charming, and once he seduces you then you're infected and turn into a vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>The original isn't handsome or charming, and he doesn't seduce, he forces. He's more like a mentally-oriented Anakim - your will breaks under him because he's too strong, and he destroys you.<br /> <br /> (Though now I quite like the idea of ChroD's Dracula being a Beast, and while he helped found the Ordo Dracul, it was more by facilitating the right vampires meeting each other.<br /> <br /> Having said that, Infection sounds like a viable basis for a Family, though I think a focus on mental disarrangement (mental illness, gothic madness, being sucked into someone's orbit) is more distinct from the ones we have.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149403#post1149403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always found that to be a weird interpretation of the Gorgons. I feel like Alluring is more Makara.</div> </div> </div> </div>An observation I made about Makara once was that sea monsters are not generally dangerous unless you go into (or at least right next to) the sea - their world is inimical, but you have to take one step into it yourself for it to harm you. Which is the reason for the deep sea treasure imagery - it's the Family where you fear the big risk is <i>not</i> followed by the big reward, but the big comeuppance. Allure works with that too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For now, I am more curious about that Hunger for Secrets, which sounds like THE go-to Hunger for the stereotypical Ugallu for me so far. </div> </div> </div>Matt described the money hit as being the point where the person with the secret realises that someone else knows. That could be blackmail, or it could be creepy hints being dropped - but it makes me wonder if straight up exposure might not count - if the secret has to remain a secret for it to work.<br /> <br /> I agree though - it sounds great for Ugallu.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 10-13-2017, 11:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T08:23:47-07:00","id":1149425,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149417#post1149417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The original isn't handsome or charming, and he doesn't seduce, he forces. He's more like a mentally-oriented Anakim - your will breaks under him because he's too strong, and he destroys you.</div> </div> </div> </div> Damn you pop-culture osmosis <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> still there's plenty of seductive vampires out there to link into fear of infection. Along with slasher movies where sex leads directly to death. And real life STDs I suppose.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149417#post1149417\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Having said that, Infection sounds like a viable basis for a Family, though I think a focus on mental disarrangement (mental illness, gothic madness, being sucked into someone's orbit) is more distinct from the ones we have.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be part of it, along with infection by ideas &quot;if you play satanic video games you'll become an atheist!&quot;. But I wouldn't want to outright exclude physical forms of infection like regular plague or zombie bites.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T08:26:20-07:00","id":1149427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149425#post1149425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could be part of it, along with infection by ideas &quot;if you play satanic video games you'll become an atheist!&quot;. But I wouldn't want to outright exclude physical forms of infection like regular plague or zombie bites.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fundamentally, the fear that something can <i>change you</i>, whether you want it or not. That works for physical, psychological, intellectual, or social vectors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T11:21:27-07:00","id":1149480,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149403#post1149403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For now, I am more curious about that Hunger for Secrets, which sounds like THE go-to Hunger for the stereotypical Ugallu for me so far.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is discussed briefly in the Ugallu Whisper description in the splat write up.<br /> <br /> @SunlessNick: it doesn't have to remain secret, but exposing it can be more sating depending on the Beast. Some Whispers never reveal a secret beyond themselves and their victims, whether to mitigate harm...or to store up leverage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":192,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","user":"Yossarian","date":". 10-14-2017, 02:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T13:04:01-07:00","id":1149503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yossarian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149480#post1149480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">@SunlessNick: it doesn't have to remain secret, but exposing it can be more sating depending on the Beast. Some Whispers never reveal a secret beyond themselves and their victims, whether to mitigate harm...or to store up leverage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the extra data.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T13:57:40-07:00","id":1149531,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wormwood</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149403#post1149403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have always found that to be a weird interpretation of the Gorgons. I feel like Alluring is more Makara. Gorgons should not be pretty, or popular, imo. Famous, sure, succesful and envied, no problem. But not 'popular' as in 'adored, has fans, is admired as a person', But then, that's just me, I guess.<br /> <br /> The fear of becoming 'infected' (e.g. the aforementioned 'fallen woman') is different from disgust. So I can definitly see potential there.<br /> For now, I am more curious about that Hunger for Secrets, which sounds like THE go-to Hunger for the stereotypical Ugallu for me so far.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Well, the original Gorgon turned people to stone because they were unspeakably hideous. But over time, the myth has changed to making this an activated power, with the Gorgon's eyes starting to glow as they emit death rays.<br /> <br /> As long as the modern Gorgon isn't actively trying to petrify you, it's fine for you to look at them. And they're usually more attractive than the myths describe them as.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://images4.alphacoders.com/678/thumb-1920-678517.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-13-2017, 04:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T14:13:41-07:00","id":1149537,"title":"","content":"Go back far enough, and Medusa is a cthonic sea goddess who heals people, and was later demonized. So, originally, the Gorgons aren't even gorgons, but closer to Sirens! There's a lot of wiggle room in the Families. I don't put much faith in certain critters = certain Families. It is true that families have specific birthrights only they have, and without other Beasts, can only learn the four affinity Atavisms. So, I really focus on those five things for families, to get a feel of them. <br /> <br /> But Hungers? Ehh.... Considering that you are supposed to personalize all the existing Hungers for your PC anyways, and there's no real mechanic tied to a Hunger... its not really that hard to just ignore the split of different kinds of Hunger in the first place, and just personalize the idea you want to hunt in the first place. So, new hunger idea leaves me bleh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T14:38:47-07:00","id":1149542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149531#post1149531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, the original Gorgon turned people to stone because they were unspeakably hideous. But over time, the myth has changed to making this an activated power, with the Gorgon's eyes starting to glow as they emit death rays.</div> </div> </div> </div>Likewise, the reflection thing was originally Perseus tracking Medusa by her reflection in his bronze shield because it would have been just a blur - enough to tell where she was, but not enough to discern her appearance.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As long as the modern Gorgon isn't actively trying to petrify you, it's fine for you to look at them. And they're usually more attractive than the myths describe them as. </div> </div> </div>Sometime, I will play a Gorgon and rationalise this as the curse wearing off.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T14:39:09-07:00","id":1149543,"title":"","content":"As Atavisms tied to the new Families go, I tend to assume the ones tied to Fear of the Other might be related to impersonation and shapeshifting. It is an area corebook Atavisms were sorely deficient in (apart from Siren's Treacherous Song allowing voice imitation) despite being a typical 'physical' power of certain mythic monsters. Such powers would have a solid thematic and mystical tie with the infiltration and social contamination paranoia Fear of the Other often expresses. Another possible expression might be charming and seduction, but Alien Allure and Siren's Song already deal with this to a good degree. I'm not sure how 'physical' powers such as Atavisms that are supposed to express bodily features of the Horror (if under a flexible dream logic) might otherwise express the supernatural aspects of social paranoia, other possible expressions of the concept seem best dealt with by Nightmares.<br /> <br /> As it concerns Atavisms tied to Fear of Confinement, I suppose web-slinging or spitting sticky goo would be an excellent fit, and in a reverse way so would the ability to become extremely flexible and if wished constrict a victim. Another good fit in this regard would be manifesting entrapping tentacles or multiple limbs, but Monster from the Deep already covers this to a good degree, so I'm not sure how to deal with the overlap issue. A third good idea would be a paralyzing gaze.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1949,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","user":"Irioth","date":". 10-14-2017, 10:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T15:33:58-07:00","id":1149552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SunlessNick</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149542#post1149542\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sometime, I will play a Gorgon and rationalise this as the curse wearing off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fortunately the human doesn't have to have any physical similarities to the Horror. Medusa could easily make herself at home in the soul of a handsome man. And the Primordial Dream aspect allows you to have both an ancient and horrifying Gorgon as well as the new wave pretty and only incidentally harmful one in the same setting.<br /> <br /> I'd guess that somewhere in the Player's Guide would be Merits to allow some aspect of the Horror to shine through your physical aspect, though. If not it seems like something easy to do, you could crib a little from Changeling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 10-13-2017, 06:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T16:36:54-07:00","id":1149563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149552#post1149552\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Fortunately the human doesn't have to have any physical similarities to the Horror.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, I meant a Gorgon Gorgon, not a Namtaru.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T06:18:35-07:00","id":1149663,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Irioth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149543#post1149543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As it concerns Atavisms tied to Fear of Confinement, I suppose web-slinging or spitting sticky goo would be an excellent fit, and in a reverse way so would the ability to become extremely flexible and if wished constrict a victim. Another good fit in this regard would be manifesting entrapping tentacles or multiple limbs, but Monster from the Deep already covers this to a good degree, so I'm not sure how to deal with the overlap issue. A third good idea would be a paralyzing gaze.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Actually, Monster from the Deep is a straight up attack. You slam the target with a tentacle, or similar appendage.<br /> <br /> I've actually wanted a web / goo based Atavism for a while now. Tried to home brew it twice, but couldn't think of proper mechanics for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1394,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","user":"Nyrufa","date":". 10-14-2017, 09:21 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T07:04:34-07:00","id":1149671,"title":"","content":"Webbing feels straight forward to me.<br /> <br /> Normal: Roll Dexterity + Firearms vs Dexterity + Athletics, on a success you apply the immobilized tilt, characters may try to break free like normal. The Durability of your webbing is equal to Lair.<br /> <br /> Low Satiety: Anyone caught may make at most Stamina attempts to escape, after that they're physically tired, paralysed by venom, psychically compelled to give in. Whatever fits your charachter.<br /> <br /> Satiety Expenditure: You make a medium burst as per the autofire rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T07:50:33-07:00","id":1149684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nyrufa</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149663#post1149663\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, Monster from the Deep is a straight up attack. You slam the target with a tentacle, or similar appendage.</div> </div> </div> </div>On second thoughts, you're actually right. Monster from the Deep is a tentacle-based damaging Atavism, so there is plenty of room for a tentacle-based entrapping Atavism tied to the Fear of Confinement. Of course, it might be tentacles, multiple limbs, constricting spires.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-14T11:10:00-07:00","id":1149737,"title":"","content":"Well, you <i>can </i>grapple things with Monster from the Deep, but it severly eats away at your Satiety.<br /> So yeah, something that helps constricting and stuff would be fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8542-wormwood","name":"Wormwood","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8542_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1198"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T09:01:41-08:00","id":1157944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haberdasher</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1149297#post1149297\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At this point, I think we could really benefit from a Dual Hungers Merit. I think it could give a lot of wiggle room for character concepts: a Beast like the one you described above could be an Enabler/Nemesis, tempting people to break their taboos and then humiliating them as punishment, or a Beast with the Hungers of Transgressions/Ruin, who loves watching people ruin their reputations by giving in to their darkest, most shameful desires.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dearly wish we can get a Dual Hunger Merit in the Player's Guide, since it would enable many character concepts. In the meanwhile, here's my own proposal:<br /> <br /> <b>Broad Palate (\u2022\u2022\u2022)</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite:</b> Beast, Composure 3, Resolve 3<br /> <b>Effect:</b> This Merit gives your character a second Hunger, an alternate method of gaining Satiety.<br /> <b>Drawback:</b> The Horror's expanded palate makes it gluttonous. Add +1 to the character's threshold for Low Satiety for the purpose of Inflicting Nightmares (i.e. the character's Horror goes wandering for sustenance at Satiety 4 or lower). Additionally, the character adds +1 to the threshold for High Satiety for the purpose of gaining and resolving Satiety Conditions (i.e. the character must reach Satiety 8 to resolve the Sated Condition and gain the Gorged Condition).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1949-irioth","name":"Irioth","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"566"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-12T09:30:41-08:00","id":1157951,"title":"","content":"Will we finally get merits and things to populate Lairs with minions and props? Can there be a Lair Trait where inanimate objects in your Lair gain sentience like the Beast's Castle in Beauty and the Beast?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1157-soulgambit","name":"SoulGambit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"912"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T14:01:09-08:00","id":1158627,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SoulGambit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1148558-a-new-hunger-has-been-revealed?p=1157951#post1157951\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Will we finally get merits and things to populate Lairs with minions and props? Can there be a Lair Trait where inanimate objects in your Lair gain sentience like the Beast's Castle in Beauty and the Beast?</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, you can already represent that in part with Lair Traits - hell, you could make up a specific one like 'Animate' or something - but that would be nice to have as something with a little more distinctiveness to it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/<img class=\"bbcode-attachment js-need-data-att-update\" src=\"filedata/fetch?filedataid=423\" data-tempid=\"temp_423_1523360155059_212\" />\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10397-ajf115","name":"ajf115","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10397_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2416"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}